#
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tsan preset. The system Qt is not instrumented, so ThreadSanitizer cannot see
# the synchronisation inside it. Tests labelled tsan-safe use no Qt threading of their own; the only Qt thread in them
# is QtTest's watchdog, which QtTest starts and joins itself.
#
# Races that only uninstrumented code takes part in, such as QtTest reusing the stack memory of the watchdog's
# condition variable after joining it, are left out by ignore_noninstrumented_modules=1 in TSAN_OPTIONS
# (tests/CMakeLists.txt), not by entries here: without debug information those frames have no names to match, and CI
# has none. Entries name only exported symbols, which resolve with or without debug information.

# The watchdog thread is joined inside Qt, so ThreadSanitizer reports it as leaked.
thread:QThread::start
